Subject: [PATCH] HID: sony: apply the ShanWan quirk over USB only

SHANWAN_GAMEPAD sends output reports on the interrupt channel only. Over
Bluetooth, ShanWan controllers ignore that channel (LEDs keep blinking and
the pad disconnects after ~50 s): they want the control channel like genuine
controllers.

The quirk never triggered over Bluetooth because the BT name differs, but
with bluez/0004 the pad keeps its USB name; restrict the quirk to USB.

Tested: ShanWan named "ShanWan PS(R) Ga`epad" over BT: crisp rumble, steady
LED.
---
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-sony.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-sony.c
@@ -2183,8 +2183,14 @@
 	if (!strcmp(hdev->name, "FutureMax Dance Mat"))
 		quirks |= FUTUREMAX_DANCE_MAT;
 
-	if (!strcmp(hdev->name, "SHANWAN PS3 GamePad") ||
-	    !strcmp(hdev->name, "ShanWan PS(R) Ga`epad"))
+	/*
+	 * Only over USB: over Bluetooth, ShanWan controllers want output
+	 * reports on ctrl like genuine ones, and BlueZ may report their USB
+	 * name for cable-paired controllers.
+	 */
+	if ((quirks & SIXAXIS_CONTROLLER_USB) &&
+	    (!strcmp(hdev->name, "SHANWAN PS3 GamePad") ||
+	     !strcmp(hdev->name, "ShanWan PS(R) Ga`epad")))
 		quirks |= SHANWAN_GAMEPAD;
 
 	sc = devm_kzalloc(&hdev->dev, sizeof(*sc), GFP_KERNEL);
